# LLMD extension
lang: typescript

// Spec for this extension, written in its own format. Format rules: @skills/llmd/SKILL.md
// The plan is intent, the code is the proof: a step says what to change, and once it's built it leaves the spec.

## [x] The plan knows the code
@src/code.ts
  : CodeSymbol
    - kind: vscode.SymbolKind
    - detail: string
    - at: vscode.Location
  - symbolsOf(uri: vscode.Uri) -> Promise<Map<string, CodeSymbol> | undefined>
    - a file's symbols by plain name, from its language's extension: the top level and the members of classes and the like
    - kept until the file changes; no answer isn't kept
  - codeHover(at: vscode.Location) -> Promise<vscode.MarkdownString | undefined>
    - the hover the file's own language shows on the symbol: signature and doc comment
  - watchCode(context: vscode.ExtensionContext)
    - forgets a file's symbols when it changes in an editor or on disk, and fires onDidChangeCode once things settle

@src/symbols.ts
  - claims(nodes: OutlineNode[]) -> Claim[]
    - the types and methods under every unit, not only done steps', with newFile for a + unit
  - isNew(c: Claim, names?) -> boolean
    - everything in a + unit, or a name its @ file's symbols don't have; no symbols is no verdict
  - unitAbove(text: string, line: number) -> string | undefined
    - the unit whose members the line lists, directly or under one of its types; undefined on a logic line

@src/extension.ts
  - newRanges(doc: vscode.TextDocument) -> Promise<vscode.Range[]>
    - the names isNew says the step adds, colored with gitDecoration.addedResourceForeground
  - hover(doc: vscode.TextDocument, pos: vscode.Position)
    - the real hover on a type or method the code has, "New: ... has no X yet" on one it doesn't
  - findDefinition(doc: vscode.TextDocument, pos: vscode.Position)
    - a type or method the code has opens in its file; a name in a logic line still goes to the spec
  - completeNames(doc: vscode.TextDocument, pos: vscode.Position)
    - a new "- " line under a unit offers codeCompletions of its file
  - codeCompletions(doc: vscode.TextDocument, unit: string)
    - the file's real types and methods, written the spec's way: "save()" and ": Store"
  - resolveCompletion(item: vscode.CompletionItem)
    - a picked completion gets the symbol's codeHover as its docs
  ! a method that exists in its @ file is never colored as new
  ! every method under a +unit is new, without asking a language server
  // start from symbolsOf: the drift check already asks the file's language server for its symbols

## [x] Done is proven by the code
~@src/snapshot.ts
~@src/cli.ts
  // the CLI only had llmd snapshot
~@.npmignore

@src/code.ts
  - missing(root: vscode.Uri, lines: string[]) -> Promise<string[]>
    - every unit has to exist, and every type and method its file's symbols can vouch for

@src/extension.ts
  - a ✓ Done lens on a ticked step the code backs, "Not in the code yet: ..." on one it doesn't
  - ~driftProblems(doc), ~driftProblem(doc, c), ~symbolsOf(uri): symbolsOf lives in code.ts now

@src/run.ts
  - done(run: Run)
    - refuses a step that isn't ticked, or that the code doesn't back yet, without waiting on the warning
    - takes the step out of its spec and keeps the file; the run becomes the step's review
  - post(run: Run)
    - a ticked step taken out of the spec by hand is done too
  - commit(run: Run, message: string)
    - the step's files and its spec
  - nextSteps(root: vscode.Uri)
    - the open steps of the plans in .llmd/
  - newFeature()
    - makes a plan in .llmd/<name>.llmd
  - ~accept(run), ~pickSnapshot(root), ~snapshots(root), ~openFeature()

@package.json
  - llmd.done in place of llmd.accept; no llmd.openFeature, no hidden drafts folder, no bin or prepack

@.github/workflows/release.yml
  - releases only llmd.vsix
// decided: tick + proof: Claude still ticks a built step, and the code has to back the tick; a tick it doesn't back shows what's missing
// decided: Done opens the run's review, with its changes, the commit and Next

## [x] Refurbish the run tab
@media/run.js
  - status()
    - Done, "Ticked, not in the code yet", or "Built, review and mark done"
  - drawBar()
    - ✓ Done in Accept's place, once the step is ticked and the code backs it
  - drawStep()
    - under a ticked step the code doesn't back, the list of what's missing
@media/run.css
  - .note.missing and ul.missing in the warning color
// decided: keep the drawn step on the left

## [x] The skill and the guide say the new way
@skills/llmd/SKILL.md
@docs/guide.md
@README.md
  - the plan is intent, the code is the proof: no Current state, snapshots, fold, drafts or CLI
  - Claude ticks a built step and leaves it; the user marks it done, which takes it out of the spec
  - the guide's editor help covers the green "new" names, real completion, hover and Ctrl+click
